    """Applied IDs a rollback must keep: `retained` plus their applied deps.

    Keeping a change while removing anything it depends on would leave a
    released artifact without its prerequisite, so retention is transitive.
    Only *applied* dependencies are followed: an unapplied dependency was never
    released, so rollback has nothing to undo for it and the walk stops there.
    The graph is already known acyclic when this runs, so no visited guard is
    needed beyond the applied filter; the closure still terminates.
